From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v2 runner: fused GDN/KDA spec-decode metadata build

VLLM_GLM5_PROLOGUE_FUSE (default 0 = upstream body, byte for byte;
_GDN sub-switch defaults to 1 and only bisects). Port of the GDN part of
Morrowmake's vllm/v1/worker/gpu/prologue_fuse.py. In steady DFlash decode
(every row a spec row, padded rows empty at the back, full cudagraphs) each
GDNAttentionMetadataBuilder.build call drops one pinned HtoD, two CPU-bool
mask indexings of CUDA tensors, an unused sub, an arange, six copy_ and five
fill_ in favour of one Triton launch that writes the same persistent
buffers. Integer index tensors only: bit-identical. Any other batch shape
falls back to the upstream body.

